BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New Voices | Panel Discussion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260711T163000
UID:3b3add34e5edeff8baced4162e783d0b@petalumaartscenter.org
DESCRIPTION:Max Jones | Feasting New Voices | Panel Discussion $15 Member\
 ; $20 Non-Member Join us for an inspiring afternoon at the Petaluma Arts C
 enter for Teaching As Art Practice \, a panel discussion exploring the dyn
 amic relationship between teaching and creative practice. Drawing from Ari
 stotle’s quote\, “Those who can\, do\; those who understand\, teach\,
 ” this conversation brings together artist educators from across the Nor
 th Bay to discuss how teaching art shapes\, challenges\, and enriches thei
 r own artistic work. Through personal experiences and shared perspectives\
 , panelists will reflect on mentorship\, creative process\, pedagogy\, and
  the evolving role of educators within contemporary art communities. The p
 anel features professors and teachers from Sonoma State University\, Colle
 ge of Marin\, and Santa Rosa Junior College. Moderated by New Voices Curat
 or Emma Logan \, this engaging discussion offers insight into the intersec
 tion of artmaking\, education\, and community connection. [data-website-co
 mponent-id="3537fedecfe0a2f02f00"] { } [data-website-component-id="3537fed
 ecfe0a2f02f00"] .sqs-html-content { } #block-3537fedecfe0a2f02f00 { mix-bl
 end-mode: var(--tweak-text-block-blend )\; border-radius: var(--tweak-text
